# Data Agent Project Rules

## Documentation Requirements
- Maintain `.agent-memory/` documentation files (`productContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `progress.md`) in sync with code changes.
- Document all new API endpoints, environment variables, and module interfaces.

## Architecture & Code Style
- Follow the 4-layer decoupled architecture defined in `.agent-memory/systemPatterns.md`.
- Maintain strict separation of concerns between tick ingestion, storage, analytics, AI reasoning, and messaging.
- Use defensive imports for optional third-party SDKs (`google.cloud.bigquery`, `google.cloud.storage`).
- All file write operations targeting shared assets (e.g. `bayesian_priors.json`) MUST use atomic file replacement (write to temp file then rename).

## Testing Standards
- All new features must include corresponding unit and integration tests in `tests/test_vps_*.py`.
- Run tests using `pytest -o pythonpath=.` to ensure module resolution across environments.

## Security Rules
- NEVER commit secrets, API keys (`XAI_API_KEY`, `OPENWA_API_KEY`), or Pocket Option SSID session tokens (`PO_SSID`) to version control.
- Use `.env` files and environment variables for all sensitive configuration parameters.
